QA of a new GAMOS version with the tutorials (see the GAMOS User's Guide, Appendix A,
"Comparing two GAMOS versions with the tutorials"). No ROOT is needed: StatTest/statTest.py
uses only the Python 3 standard library.

EXAMPLE: PETTutorial/exercise2/exercise2b

0. Configuration file exercise2b.qaref: lines of the text output and histograms to compare, and tests to use.
   It is created only once for each exercise, from the output of one job and its CSV histogram files:
cd PETTutorial/exercise2
gamos exercise2b.in > out.exercise2b
sh buildQA.exercise2b.sh        (or e.g. sh ../../buildQA.countTracks.sh exercise2b)
   which calls StatTest/prepareQATemplate.py (one template for each kind of lines)
   and StatTest/prepareQA.py (joins the templates and adds the histograms)

1. With the OLD release, build the reference files, merging 10 jobs
cd GAMOS_OLD/tutorials/PETTutorial
bash ../run1qa.sh exercise2 exercise2b
=> exercise2/ref.out.exercise2b
=> exercise2/ref.gammaSD.exercise2b.csv
=> exercise2/ref.hits.exercise2b.csv

2. With the NEW release, build the reference files in the same way
cd GAMOS_NEW/tutorials/PETTutorial
bash ../run1qa.sh exercise2 exercise2b

3. Compare them (gamos is not run)
cd GAMOS_NEW/tutorials
export GAMOS_RELEASE_OLD=GAMOS_OLD/tutorials
bash run1qa.sh PETTutorial exercise2 exercise2b
=> PETTutorial/exercise2/qatest.summary.*          tests that failed
=> PETTutorial/exercise2/qatest.report.*.pdf       plots of the histograms

All tutorials: bash runAllN with each release, then bash runAllQA with the new one, and bash showQA.sh
(the PDF viewer is evince, or the one set in the environment variable QA_PDF_VIEWER)
